#
# rosconsole config for the robot_localization EKF nodes (vitulus_ekf_outdoor.launch:
# ekf_wheel_odometry, ekf_wheel_nav_odometry; ekf_indoor.launch), set per node via
# <env name="ROSCONSOLE_CONFIG_FILE">.
#
# Every /set_pose (the dock seed, the GPS/heading bridge, navi_transform re-anchors)
# makes ros_filter.cpp print "Received set_pose request with value" + the whole
# PoseWithCovarianceStamped at INFO (~20 lines each, many per minute) into
# rosout.log and the node stdout log. The upstream code logs it through the
# package's default logger, so the narrowest logger rosconsole can address is
# ros.robot_localization: INFO of these EKF nodes is off, WARN/ERROR stay
# (lost sensors, bad covariance, transform failures). The other INFO lines of the
# EKF ("Enabling filter...", "Toggling filter measurement filtering") go with it.
# navsat_transform is NOT under this config - its datum/UTM INFO stays.
#
# This replaces the former local patch of other/robot_localization (INFO -> DEBUG
# in ros_filter.cpp); robot_localization itself is plain upstream again.
#
# Same as the default /opt/ros/noetic/share/ros/config/rosconsole.config plus the
# one line for robot_localization. Revert: delete the <env> lines in the launches.
#
log4j.logger.ros=INFO
log4j.logger.ros.roscpp.superdebug=WARN
log4j.logger.ros.robot_localization=WARN
